[ system ]
    You decide one thing in a dark-fantasy Skyrim roleplay. The player's side beat this enemy in a fight and left them
    alive; they have just recovered enough to fight again. Judge from the enemy's character, the fight, and what the
    player said to them while they were beaten: do they stand down toward the player for good, or will they fight again?
    Mercy, persuasion, fear, gratitude or a promise can make them stand down; pride, hatred, orders or a failed talk keep
    them hostile.

    Answer with one line of JSON only, no other text:
    {"decision": "<stand_down | hostile>", "reason": "<one short line>"}
[ end system ]

[ user ]
    {% set npc = formid_to_uuid(npcId) %}
    The enemy: {{ decnpc(npc).name }}
    {{ render_character_profile("short_inline", npc) }}
    {% if location != "" %}Where: {{ location }}{% endif %}

    What was said between them and the player since the fight:
    {% if dialogue != "" %}{{ dialogue }}{% else %}(nothing was said){% endif %}
[ end user ]
